Thanks to everyone for the massive responce.  Looked like everyone had
the right idea, 
and/or the right UNIX answer, but:

As it turns out:

The ulimits were set correctly on the UNIX side.  
The DBA added a line in the users' .profile that called an oracle
environmental config file
 (/usr/local/bin/oraenv) that redefined the users specific ulimits.

All better now.

Ulimits, ulimits, we don't need no stinkin' ulimits!

