Subject: SUMMARY - Connect BA350 Array to PMAZC-AA
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078613510565

Hello Everyone

Thanks for all the suggestions I received from this group.
Everyone basically said the same thing that they had 
already connected a BA35* to a PMAZC-AA SCSI 
turbo controller inside a DEC 3000/600S running UNIX 3.2d.

SETUP
-----
Once the PMAZC-AA has been installed and configured into 
your server, you can then connect the BA350 to one of the 
two SCSI channels. Then using the documentation 
provided you can issue some basic commands to view and 
configure the PMAZC-AA card from the console prompt.

e.g >>>>  t tc0 cnfg 

The command above examines the PMAZC-AA card on SCSI 0 and 
displays some information about what is attatched to this 
card.

Once the drives are showing up, then you can treat them as 
you would any new disk and rebuild the kernel. See "Booting 
from GENVMUNIX and rebuilding a kernel" in you UNIX 
documentation.


