From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Jun 20 00:13:05 1997
From: Shane Caple <scaple () banda ! ntu ! edu ! au>
Date: Fri, 20 Jun 1997 00:13:05 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: how to configure a de500-aa card?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078613510532

thanks to everyone who answered!

for a de500-aa with device name 'ewb0' ...
---

at the console prompt ('>>>'), type this:
  
  set ewb0_mode Auto

the card will then negotiate both speed and duplex with the switch or hub.
(auto-negotiate is supported for DE500-AA, but not DE500-XA.)


ALSO


at the console prompt ('>>>'), type this:

  set ewb0_mode ?

this gives a list of the different options. with different mode strings, you
can setup full/half duplex, auto-negotiation, etc.

---
Shane (still learning the ropes).

