Quite some time ago, I have changed COM1_BAUD from 9600 to 38400
for I forgot what reason.  Apparently, both the DU installation
and the ARC are resetting serial lines to 9600, so after:
>>> set com1_baud 9600
everything was all right.  Yes, I've been using a VT because
there is no VGA card in AS2100.  It would have never occurred to
me if it wasn't for an older colleague who told me to check the
baud rate.  So, it wasn't firmware nor ECU problem.

Advice: never change baud rate from 9600 on serial line #1.

I would like to thank atoalu2@ato.abb.se (Andreas Lundgren) for
his kind offer of ECU1.9.

Greetings!

