From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Jun 06 00:21:41 1997
From: loi huynh <lhuynh () newscorp ! com ! au>
Date: Fri, 06 Jun 1997 00:21:41 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: daemon.log
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078613510268

Thanks go to "Kevin Oberman" <oberman@es.net> who responsed to
my query regarding Lame delegation in my daemon.log.

My sincere apology to those whose mail clients could not understand
S/MIME.

ORIGINAL QUESTION:

>We have a DU 3.2c running named and I found the following messages in
> the daemon.log but not sure what it means:
>
> ----extract from daemon.log with domain name and IP replaced--------
> Jun  4 01:53:13 wombat named[4827]: Lame delegation to 'blablabla.com'

> from [ an ip address ] (server for 'blablabla.com'?) on query on name
> 'blablabla.com'
>
> Jun  4 01:53:28 wombat named[4827]: Lame delegation to
> 'blablabla.com.au' from [another ip address] (server for
> 'blablabla.com.au'?) on query on name 'blablabla.com.au'
>-------------------------------------------------------------------------

>

ANSWER:

Kevin pointed out that it is standard BIND notification during foreign
domain lookup:

> This is a standard BIND notification that your server looked up the
> name server for some foreign domain, sent it a query, and found that
> the system was not a name server for that domain. This is a DNS
> configuration problem at the foreign domain and out of your control.
> (If the foreign domain IS under your control fix it!)

There is no reason to concern about these messages.  He mentioned that
there is a latest release of BIND at (http://www.isc.org/bind.html)

Since the message logged was not critical, I have no intention of
updating BIND,
therefore I can't comment on the process or any other associated issues
involved.

Sincerely,

Loi Huynh.

