Subject: SUMMARY: Summary of tlz drives??
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078613510259


The Question:

> 
> Can some one give the rundown on capacity and tape lengths that can be
> used in the following drives?
> 
> TLZ04
> TLZ06
> TLZ07
> TLZ09
> 

The Answer:


TLZ04 uses 60M 4mm DAT cartridges whose capacity is 1.3GB.  It cannot use 
90M nor 120M cartridges, nor can it read 60M tapes written by TLZ06 or 
TLZ07/09 drives IF HARDWARE COMPRESSION WAS USED TO WRITE THE TAPE.

TLZ06 uses 90M 4mm DAT cartridges whose capacity is 2.0GB (w/o
compression).  It cannot use 120M cartridges.

TLZ07/09 uses 120M 4mm DDS-2 DAT cartridges whose capacity is 4.0GB (w/o
compression). 

The TLZ06 and TLZ07 drives do provide hardware compression to
approximately double the tape's capacity.

