had been installed by an earlier patch, osf410-400106_v40b. Prior to
the installation of duv40bas00003-1997042 the abbreviated output from
a setld -i was:

OSFPAT00000000410    installed  Patch Tools (- Required -)
OSFPAT00000001410    installed  Patch Tools (- Required -)

After an unsuccessful installation attempt, the setld output was: 

OSFPAT00000000410    installed  Patch Tools (- Required -)
OSFPAT00000001410    installed  Patch Tools (- Required -)
OSFPAT00000002410    corrupt    Patch Tools (- Required -)

I received a response and _solution_ from Martin Moore at DEC. The
meat of his response follows:

> We've seen this happen a couple times before and the problem is
> under investigation.  You can workaround it by manually installing
> the Patch Tools subset, OSFPAT00000002410. [Then] do:
>
>	setld -l . OSFPAT00000002410
> ...
>
> Then run dupatch again, and the patches should install.

I did as instructed, and the patches installed fine.

Thanks Martin!

