Hi DU Admins

I asked:

> Is the minimum firmware needed for 3.2g the same as for 3.2c?
> Or to put it another way: when upgrading from 3.2c to 3.2g is it 
> necessary to upgrade the firmware?

The answer is no to the first and probably to the second.  The
minimum firmware for 3.2c is v3.3 and for 3.2g it is v3.6.

Thanks to Alex Kok, Dr. Tom Blinn and Matthew Calthrop.  Here
is the last part of Alex's reply:

> My advice is to upgrade to the latest version (the 3.9 CD in this
> case) regardless of OS version. The 3.9 FW upgrade is quite 
> easy, but be sure to read the installation instructions, some
> (very few) specific Alphas have some (very few) possible problems
> which I (quite unlikely) ran into once. You don't want that so 
> read the docs first! They are on the CD in text and Postscript
> formats.


Thanks
Ian

