To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] HP X Terminal Logins
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078613510123

Hi Du Admins

I asked a question about HP X Terms sometimes locking up when 
attempting to connect to our alphas running DU 3.2c.  This was
my second attempt to find a solution to this problem.

The only reply I got was from Lee Hughes who made this suggestion:

   first thing I'd check is the network, make sure you not loosing packets,
   X uses alot of UDP transport, so try this first!

This isn't the problem in our case.

I managed to find the solution myself.  There's a patch for xdm to fix 
this.  It is patch ID OSF350X-005 contained within patch kit 
ssrt0368u_v32c.

I looked for a patch a few months ago using the web patch service
but didn't find anything.  This time I just used ftp to download the
READMEs for all the DU 3.2c patches and grepped for xdm.

I haven't installed the patch yet because it looks like there's 
an alternative.  There isn't an equivalent patch for 3.2g so I
assume that 3.2g includes it.  So we could upgrade to 3.2g instead.


Cheers
Ian

